\f0\fs24 \cf0 # IIH AI Demonstrator\
\
## Status\
\
Demonstration prototype only.\
\
- Synthetic data only\
- Not validated for clinical use\
- No autonomous diagnosis\
- No autonomous treatment recommendation\
- No autonomous admission, discharge, or transfer decision\
- Human clinician retains responsibility for all clinical decisions\
\
## Purpose\
\
This Streamlit application demonstrates a deterministic, clinician-in-the-loop\
workflow for adult presentations with confirmed, uncertain, or non-confirmed\
papilloedema / possible idiopathic intracranial hypertension (IIH).\
\
The system separates:\
\
1. Structured intake\
2. Validation of required workflow data\
3. Deterministic rule-engine evaluation\
4. Clinician review, sign-off, and override\
\
## Included demonstrations\
\
- Potential visual threat escalation\
- Hypertensive emergency flag\
- CVST / secondary venous pathway\
- Missing venography hard stop\
- Typical and atypical IIH candidate states\
- Abnormal CSF pathway\
- Pseudopapilloedema follow-up safeguards\
- NOPH contact de-duplication and recontact triggers\
\
## Safety boundary\
\
The application is an educational workflow demonstrator. It must not be used\
with real patient data or as a substitute for clinical assessment, local policy,\
specialist advice, diagnostic imaging interpretation, or clinical governance.\
\
## Run locally\
\
```bash\
python3 -m venv .venv\
source .venv/bin/activate\
pip install -r requirements.txt\
streamlit run app.py\
```}